      "p0001-n0009-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "How to analyze the music objectively?"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000010",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0002-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u5fae\u4fe1\u516c\u4f17\u53f7\uff1a\u6570\u5b66\u6a21\u578b"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000011",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "heading",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0010-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Summary"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000012",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0011-l0000",
      "p0001-n0011-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Music is a form of art that profoundly in\ufb02uences humans and societies. Given the four data sets, we are motivated to develop a series of objective measurements to analyze the music from four perspectives."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000013",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0012-l0000",
      "p0001-n0012-l0001",
      "p0001-n0012-l0002",
      "p0001-n0012-l0003",
      "p0001-n0012-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "First of all, the measurement of music in\ufb02uence between artists is given by the combination of three indicators: 1) the indicator related to artists active in one certain decade being followed by artists active in other decades, 2) the indicator related to artists of one certain genre being followed by artists of other genres, and 3) the out-degree of the in\ufb02uencers. A weighted directed graph \ud43a(\ud449, \ud438) is constructed to represent the in\ufb02uence network, where an edge is directed from the in\ufb02uencer to the"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000014",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0003-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u5fae\u4fe1\u53f7\uff1aMATHmodels"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000015",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0012-l0005"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "follower. Therefore, the calculated in\ufb02uence between the two artists is the weight of a directed edge."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000016",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0000",
      "p0001-n0013-l0001",
      "p0001-n0013-l0002",
      "p0001-n0013-l0003",
      "p0001-n0013-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Secondly, the music similarity is quanti\ufb01ed. Since the provided data sets full_music_data contains high-dimensional data, thus the dimension reduction is needed. We are motivated to use the modi\ufb01ed randomly distributed embedding (RDE) framework to take good advantage of interaction information of high-dimensional data. Moreover, the Bayes error rate is used to identify whether the distributions of within-genre and between-genre are signi\ufb01cantly di\ufb00erent."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000017",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0014-l0000",
      "p0001-n0014-l0001",
      "p0001-n0014-l0002",
      "p0001-n0014-l0003",
      "p0001-n0014-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Thirdly, we analyzed two kinds of roles of musical characteristics by examining the \ud45d-values from Kruskal-Wallis test. We removed each characteristic one at a time, and compared the \ud45d-values before and after the certain characteristics is removed. From the experiment results, the most in\ufb02uential characteristics in distinguishing genres are Energy, Valence, and Speechiness. The most contagious characteristics among artists are Acousticness, Danceability, and Valence."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000018",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0001",
